  <class_name>SetSiteWaterMainsTemperature</class_name>
  <display_name>Set Site Water Mains Temperature</display_name>
  <description>Set the Site:WaterMainsTemperature object to have:
- Calculation Method: 'Correlation' or 'Schedule'

If Schedule:
- user-supplied schedule

If 'Correlation':
- Annual Average Outdoor Air Temperature (C): user-supplied
- Maximum Difference in Monthly Average Outdoor Air Temperature (C): user-supplied

There is an Excel spreadsheet in the 'resources' folder to help in caculating the correlation coefficients.</description>
  <modeler_description>For the 'Correlation' options, it's easy to calculate those using the .stat file that comes with EPW files.

Default values for Correlation are for New York City - JFK Airport.

See Engineering Reference Guide, Water Systems - Water Mains Temperature for more info
Correlation is based on Craig Christensen and Jay Burch and is described in Hendron et al (2004)
http://bigladdersoftware.com/epx/docs/9-0/engineering-reference/water-systems.html#water-mains-temperatures</modeler_description>
  <arguments>
    <argument>
      <name>calculation_method</name>
      <display_name>Calculation Method</display_name>
      <type>Choice</type>
      <required>true</required>
      <model_dependent>false</model_dependent>
      <default_value>CorrelationFromWeatherFile</default_value>
      <choices>
        <choice>
          <value>CorrelationFromWeatherFile</value>
          <display_name>CorrelationFromWeatherFile</display_name>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <value>Schedule</value>
          <display_name>Schedule</display_name>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <value>Correlation</value>
          <display_name>Correlation</display_name>
        </choice>
      </choices>
    </argument>
    <argument>
      <name>temp_sch</name>
      <display_name>Temperature Schedule Name</display_name>
      <description>Only Schedule Ruleset of Schedule Type Limits 'Temperature' will be listed. Only applies if 'Schedule' is selected above.</description>
      <type>Choice</type>
      <required>false</required>
      <model_dependent>true</model_dependent>
    </argument>
    <argument>
      <name>avg_oa_temp</name>
      <display_name>Annual Average Outdoor Air Temperature</display_name>
      <description>Only used if 'Correlation' is selected above. This is drybulb, easily calculated from .STAT file</description>
      <type>Double</type>
      <units>C</units>
      <required>false</required>
      <model_dependent>false</model_dependent>
      <default_value>12.47</default_value>
    </argument>
    <argument>
      <name>max_diff_monthly_oa_temp</name>
      <display_name>Maximum Difference in Monthly Average Outdoor Air Temperature</display_name>
      <type>Double</type>
      <units>C</units>
      <required>false</required>
      <model_dependent>false</model_dependent>
      <default_value>25.2</default_value>
    </argument>
  </arguments>
